  "how does retrieval work here, and what tradeoffs did he make?": {
    "answer": "Retrieval uses hybrid BM25 keyword search and dense cosine similarity over precomputed embeddings, fused with reciprocal rank fusion at k=60, where the top-k is a ceiling rather than a quota and a chunk scoring far under the leader is filler. The embedding call is skipped when the top BM25 score is more than 2.2 times the runner-up, and ties are broken by the better single rank rather than corpus order. He chose hybrid retrieval over dense-only because exact terms like client names, project codes, and document titles are critical in the consulting corpus, even though it costs more per query.",
